  "body": "Stacked on #2027 (merge #2027 first)\n\n## What changed\n\n- Added AccessKit `WidgetInfo` labels to painted browser tree rows (`\"Browser: {label}\"`) and eye toggles (`\"{Hide|Show} {label}\"`) in `painted.rs`.\n- Clamped the browser tree rect width in `browser_pane::browser` to the visible clip edge.\n- Added AccessKit `WidgetInfo` labels to every context-menu row in `tree_menu.rs`, using `WidgetType::Button` for items and `WidgetType::Label` with `Sense::hover()` for headers.\n- Filtered `\"Browser: \"` nodes out of `setups_declutter::shows` so persistent browser rows do not collide with Setup page label assertions.\n- Removed `BROWSER_TREE_TOP` and `BROWSER_EYE_X` from `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs`.\n- Rewrote all six browser behaviour tests to locate rows, eyes, and menu items by label instead of fixed coordinates, and recorded the design choice in `docs/decisions/1989-browser-tree-accesskit.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nPainted browser rows, eye toggles, and tree context-menu rows drew with `ui.interact` and `Painter` without attaching `WidgetInfo`. Tests had to calculate pixel coordinates with `BROWSER_TREE_TOP` and `BROWSER_EYE_X`. In `browser_pane::browser`, the top button strip inside `egui_dock`'s `ScrollArea` also widened `ui.available_width()` past `ui.clip_rect().right()`, placing the `Stock` eye center outside its clipped `interact_rect` so AccessKit clicks missed it.\n\n## Tests\n\nAll six rewritten tests failed on `base-2027` before the fix and pass after it:\n- `stock_eye_hides_the_viewport_stock_without_removing_it_from_the_document`\n- `dragging_an_operation_row_reorders_within_global_setup`\n- `operations_heading_menu_pastes_the_copied_operation`\n- `operation_type_menu_requires_confirmation`\n- `operation_menu_suppresses_and_sets_the_after_action`\n- `program_entry::the_operation_menu_adds_an_entry_and_its_own_menu_edits_it`\n\nMutation checks against `base-2027`:\n- Reverting `painted.rs` made `stock_eye_hides_the_viewport_stock_without_removing_it_from_the_document` and `dragging_an_operation_row_reorders_within_global_setup` fail; restoring it made both pass.\n- Reverting `browser_pane.rs` made `stock_eye_hides_the_viewport_stock_without_removing_it_from_the_document` fail; restoring it made it pass.\n- Reverting `tree_menu.rs` made all four `_menu_` tests fail; restoring it made them pass (`11 passed, 0 failed`).\n\nGate and checks:\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui`: 829 unit tests passed, 0 failed, 6 ignored (835 total `#[test]` kept), plus all integration suites passing.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed with 0 warnings.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: passed (`ui suites` ok, 0 failed).\n\n## Before and after screenshots\n\nMatching 1280 × 720 headless shell renders show the browser eye column, ribbon height, and theme ink. The viewport uses the shell test harness renderer. Before is `17a8c6e7608bb7078f75ec335361839712e51425`, before the stacked #2027 changes. After is `ea23b3e119cfd1abd0b43708ba56d91c5008eaf1`, the reviewed head. The screenshots live only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch.\n\n| Theme | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Horizon Day | ![Horizon Day before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/7136fd458c422fc8d81bceeecfc9eec849819173/2097/horizon-day-before.png) | ![Horizon Day after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/7136fd458c422fc8d81bceeecfc9eec849819173/2097/horizon-day-after.png) |\n| Teal Night | ![Teal Night before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/7136fd458c422fc8d81bceeecfc9eec849819173/2097/teal-night-before.png) | ![Teal Night after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/7136fd458c422fc8d81bceeecfc9eec849819173/2097/teal-night-after.png) |\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nCrates outside `camcraft-ui` did not change and were not tested outside `gate quick`. The ignored pixel snapshot tests (`egui_shell_snapshot`, `egui_shell_snapshot_light`) fail under software rendering (`#255`) and remain `#[ignore]`.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nStacked on `#2027` (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs` `BROWSER_TREE_TOP` and `crates/ui/src/egui_app/painted.rs` other functions). Other open PRs also touch `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests.rs` in different functions (`#1996`, `#2024`, `#2037`, `#2075`, `#2078`, `#2079`); whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Give painted browser tree rows, eye toggles, and context-menu rows AccessKit labels so UI tests find them without hardcoded row coordinates.\nFixes #1989\n",
